The home team put Yuki Bhambri (125th in the ATP standings), which was won last week by a challenger in Shanghai, where he beat players in the third and fourth-hundred rankings.
Somdev Devvarman (164) will be number two.
They're both players from challengers, and we've had experience from the ATP Tour, but we've convinced ourselves a lot of times that rankings don't matter in the Davis Cup.
"It decides the current form, the weather," Navratil said.
Friday's opening singles will begin at 6:30 a.m. CEST and can stretch because of the weather.
