At the same time, Kingfisher closes 60 B&Q outlets across the country
Processed by Rupert Steiner, chief correspondent for the Daily Mail
The British are said to be putting aside hammers and brushes, handing them over to employed Eastern European craftsmen to work at their home
If you're good with a hammer or a paint brush, it seems like you're in the minority today.
As Britons increasingly employ craftsmen to carry out DIY work at their home, according to the company's boss behind Screwfix B&Q.
Veronique Laury, Kingfisher's new chief executive, which owns the chain for domestic utensions, argues that a large increase in the number of traders from Eastern Europe offering services at the lowest possible prices is no longer a trend.
As a result, Kingfisher plans to open 200 additional Screwfix stores aimed at traders, closing 60 B&Q outlets.
Ms Laury argues she wants to employ more Women in B&Q stores because eight out of ten shopping decisions at the store make better halves.
Currently, the majority are male workers.
She said there was a need to reach out to growing demographic trends that depict more women's households making more home adjustments than in the past.
Ms. Laury says, "There are mostly men working in our shops.
We need to get closer to balance.
Basically, half of our customers are women who make 80% decisions about buying goods.
Women play a big role in the decision-making process.
Ms Laury, who is one of only five women at the helm of leading companies according to Britain's FTSE100 index, has also restructured her cutting-edge team to reflect equivalence between men and women's directors.
Kingfisher stands almost alone in having half the representation of women among employees, including executive and CFO.
Ms Laury argues: "It was a conscious decision - diversity is an important topic here.
So it wasn't difficult to find the good women we'd take with us.
Kingfisher announced a slump both in profits in the middle of the year and sales after the group took the cost of closing stores.
As a result of the Kingfisher trend, owned by Screwfix and B&Q, is to open 200 new stores
The December contribution of 600 crowns to pensioners is at risk.
"It's the justice of straight stomachs, it has nothing to do with human justice," said Miroslav Kalousek, vice-chairman of TOP 09, which emphasized the principle of merit.
Zbyněk Stanjura, chairman of the ODS deputies, noted that the one-time contribution sounds good, but in the long run it would be better for it to be in standard valorisation, because it would be reflected for years to come.
"We've got space to find the mechanism we'll handle it," Stanjura said.
He supported the original proposal of Minister Michaela Marksová (ČSSD), according to which it was supposed to valorize beyond the law next year.
Marks defended the subsidy by arguing that it would improve the social situation of pensioners, which, according to her, is not rosy.
According to her, a higher valuation next year would mean a budgetary impact of 5.5 billion crowns, and ministers are debating every hundreds of millions.
Prime Minister Bohuslav Sobotka (ČSSD) reminded the right that in the past the pace of valorization has been reduced.
Rapporteur Miroslav Opálka (KSČM) pointed out that the proposal does not address the reduction of real pensions in 2016 and later.
Veto of the right will significantly complicate the salary in December and perhaps make it impossible, he said.
The chairman of the ČSSD, Roman Sklenák, therefore proposed shortening the deadline for discussing the standard in the committee for ten or 20 days, even the right blocked it.
However, the committee will have a month instead of the usual two.
The bonus should cost a total of 1.73 billion crowns.
The money should go especially from the budget of the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs.
Next year, pensions are expected to rise on average by about a hundred crowns.
According to the pension amendment, the contribution should be given to people who will be entitled to a pension or part of it in December.
It could also be obtained by those whose pension expired in December before its payment.
However, they would have to apply for the surcharge in writing no later than the end of next year.
Retirementies in the Czech Republic are valorized regularly as of January, by price growth and a third of real wage growth.
This year's pension corresponds to 41.5 percent of gross wages, next year it should be 40.5 percent.
According to the state’s closing account, the state spent 314.7 billion crowns on old-age pensions last year, which was about five billion more year-on-year.
Spending on old-age pensions accounted for 26 percent of all budget spending and 46 percent of all expenses required by law.
According to data in the state's closing account, the average full old-age pension rose by 104 to 10,714 crowns.
The Czech Social Security Administration ensured the payment of 2.4 million full old-age pensions and about 17,000 proportional pensions.
Yakunin has abandoned plans for a political career, will devote himself to science.
According to Russian media, the billionaire was almost certain.
In the Federation Council, he was supposed to represent Russia's Kaliningrad region, whose governor, Nikolai Cukanov, as a candidate of the ruling United Russia party, defended his post in Sunday's elections.
According to Russian laws, senators are not elected by citizens, but are chosen by the governor from a three candidates whose names he will announce before the governor's elections.
After the election, the senator of the three candidates himself will be selected.
The complication for Yakunin was the fact that he did not live in Kaliningrad Oblast for twenty years, as required by law.
The Kremlin has found an exception for Yakunin, saying that he is an extraordinary and authorized ambassador, to whom the legal requirement of long-term residence does not apply.
It ended with the filming of the Czech comedy Tiger Theory.
The last straw in the resolution of the main character is the voluntary death of his father-in-law, who ran out of strength and patience.
Grandmother - Iva Janžurová decided her grandfather's life, old age and burial.
It is clear to Jan that he is on a similar path with his wife Olga - Eliška Balzerová.
He remembers that he used to have his own will and dreams, he wants to live with dignity and freedom again.
He longs to regain control of his life - and as a solution he chooses the escape from the previous one, Slavík said.
Bajgar wanted a comedy way to capture a certain type of relationship, in which one of the partners doesn't feel completely free.
From the beginning, it was clear that the main role would fall to Bartošek, with whom he had already collaborated on Invisible.
Nevertheless, the actor, who appeared in front of the camera after a long break associated with the convalescence after a serious illness, surprised him.
We had an appointment three years ago.
I had him read the script, and he said he liked how sad he was.
And I'm surprised he's probably a cocoon athlete.
Previously, he always asked where he would sit before filming another scene.
This time he rode a bicycle, climbing rocks and even walking up the hill.
And all this in record-breaking tropical heatwaves, the director pointed out.
According to Bartoška, the women take a tiger to turn it into a rabbit over time.
They'll pour him some feed, but they'll close the door so he wouldn't have guessed to play a tiger outside the rabbit house.
And we're trying to tell our film about that, the actor commented.
His wife, who may have a slightly negative effect on spectators, was portrayed by Eliška Balzerová.
She's not just a negative character.
She's also pleasant, intelligent, empathetic and means well.
But at the same time, she's a usurper and wants to bake her husband to death, Baigar said.
In parallel, the film also depicts the fates of Jan's married daughters Olinka and Alice - Táňa Vilhelmová and Pavla Beretová - and son-in-laws Erik and Pepík - Jiří Havelka and Jakub Kohák.
The producer of the film is Petr Erben from Logline Production, co-producers of Czech Television and Radio and Television Slovakia.
Google has pledged millions of dollars to aid refugees in Europe.
U.S. internet company Google has pledged to provide an additional 5.5 million dollars (132.6 million CZK) to organizations that help thousands of refugees flowing into Europe.
It was announced by Google.org on Tuesday, which is a charitable offshoot of this internet company.
Azerbaijan has revoked Telička's part of the visit for his criticism of human rights violations.
Czech MEP on behalf of the ANO movement Pavel Telička has postponed Thursday's trip to Baku because the Azerbaijani authorities canceled the official part of his visit today.
According to Telička, this is justified by last week's EP resolution, which criticizes human rights violations in Azerbaijan and of which Telička was a co-author.
By a decision of the Azerbaijani party, Telička lost the possibility of talks with official partners and also a visit of political prisoners, which depends on the consent of the authorities, his Brussels office explained in a press statement.
The trip, which was planned several months in advance, Telička wanted to be used to meet with the leadership of the parliament and representatives of the executive and with representatives of the democratic opposition, dissidents and political prisoners.
The EP resolution condemns "unprecedented repression against civil society in Azerbaijan."
It called on European leaders to consider sanctions against all politicians, officials and judges involved in political persecution.
The resolution was passed shortly after a recent ruling over Azerbaijani opposition journalist Khadija Ismail, who advocated the detection of corruption in government circles.
Russia has not ruled out building its air base in Syria.
Bogdanovsky did not rule out on a visit to Novosibirsk that a Russian air basis would be established in Syria in the future.
We don't have plans like that yet.
However, nothing is excluded, he said.
Russia already has an age-old naval base in Syria in the port of Tartus, which until now used more as a service and logistics center.
According to reports of the Russian press, since the beginning of August, shipments of Russian armaments and military equipment to Syria have risen.
According to Moscow, these are arms shipments resulting from valid trade agreements.
The Pentagon says the Russians intend to establish an air base near the city of Latakiya, which for the time being remains a bastion of Syrian President Bashar al-Assad.
But Washington is not entirely clear about Russia's specific military intentions in Syria, U.S. commentators agree.
U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry discussed the situation in Syria on Tuesday with Russian colleague Sergei Lavrov, his third telephone conversation in the last ten days.
Next week, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu will travel to Moscow to convey concerns over the gathering of a Russian arsenal near Israel.
White House spokesman Josh Earnest called Assad's support by Moscow a losing bet.
On Russia's policy objectives in Syria, he said they were rather unclear.
According to him, Moscow has made Syria its satellite.
It may mean that President Vladimir Putin is pursuing a long-term goal, but it's not quite clear, according to Earnest.
According to today's speculation by the Russian press, the war in Syria is supposed to be the main topic of Putin's speech at the upcoming meeting of the U.N. General Assembly in New York.
On the contrary, the Russian leader does not intend to talk about the situation in Donbas, Ukraine.
According to The New York Times, the U.S. government does not rule out that President Barack Obama could meet with the Russian president during the U.N. session.
There are so far among White House advisers.
The TASS news agency, citing Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov, reported today that Putin does not yet have a meeting with Obama on the agenda of his New York stay.
Deploy sesame oil during the gallbladder diet, hemp helps to strengthen immunity.
A good way to increase the supply of beneficial unsaturated fatty acids from these fruits is the use of extra virgin oils.
When pressing from cold seeds, all healthy substances will remain in the oil.
Therefore, these oils are also suitable as part of health diets, such as gallbladder.
Some extra virgin oils are suitable for the prevention of cardiovascular diseases.
According to the Institute of Health Information and Statistics of the Czech Republic, these have been the most common cause of death of Czechs for several years
Gallbladder inflammation mainly affects women, helps sesame oil.
If you are one of the lovers of Asian cuisine, you must not miss sesame oil in the pantry, which is part of the original recipes for exotic dishes.
Unlike most other oils, it can also be used in the heat treatment of dishes and has a number of beneficial health effects.
It is often used in the gallbladder diet.
The essential fatty acids it contains are a good prevention of the formation of gallstones.
They are 90% the cause of gallbladder inflammation, and women suffer from these difficulties three times more often than men.
In general, gallbladder problems mainly affect overweight people who do not play sports and consume a lot of animal fat.
Sesame oil can also be used successfully in the liver diet, which is very similar to the gallbladder.
If people want to take advantage of all the health benefits brought by the consumption of this oil, they should watch out for goods from exotic food stores.
Producers from Asia often use roasted seeds, which have a more pronounced taste.
The oil, however, will lose all active substances, described Ladislav Hačecký, executive director from the Czech company Bohemia Olej from Kraslice in the Sokolov region, which produces cold-pressed organic virgin oils.
The company also newly produces sesame oil and uses exclusively unroasted white sesame seeds.
In an hour, our press manages to press 8 pounds of sesame.
By mechanical pressing, the raw material is heated to a maximum of 40 degrees, and therefore the product meets the criteria for the extra-virginous designation.
At higher temperatures, there would be a loss of nutrients.
Sunflower oil thrives on heart and blood vessel diseases.
The Czech favorite among the oils is sunflower.
Jarmila Hamerská's research at Masaryk University showed that 43% of respondents prefer it in a warm kitchen.
However, it is actually not suitable for frying, already at 180 °C it is starting to burn.
It is better to use it, for example, to flavor salads and is especially useful in the diet, in which it helps in the prevention of cardiovascular diseases.
It contains a high proportion of omega 6 unsaturated fatty acids, which of all fatty acids reduce cholesterol levels the most.
With heart problems, you need to pay attention to the amount of fat and calories received overall.
For example, in one tablespoon of sunflower oil there are 62 calories, in a tablespoon of rapeseed oil there are 99 calories.
As for the energy value of food, it is important to remember that natural foods with nutritious substances are much more suitable than so-called empty calories.
They are part of industry-treated products.
Therefore, it is advisable to reach for extra virgin oils.
The sunflower lasts just like sesame and hemp for 9 months.
By storing in the fridge, the shelf life is even longer.
Old oil can be recognized especially by its bitter taste.
On the contrary, there is no turbidity at the bottom.
It's a sign that the substance wasn't chemically refined.
Hemp oil contains the most healthy acids.
Technical hemp seeds belong to so-called superfoods, and therefore hemp oil is considered the healthiest of vegetable oils.
It owes this label to the highest content of omega 3 and omega 6 unsaturated fatty acids.
These essential fatty acids cannot be produced by the body itself, and one has to take it from food.
Especially important is the intake of omega 3 fatty acids.
A study by scientists published in the European Journal of Clinical Nutrition has shown that the daily intake of this substance is insufficient.
Men in France and Greece will consume 0.6 grams, while Icelanders will accept 2.5 grams.
The recommended daily dose is 1 to 4 grams.
Hemp oil should be included in the diet as part of a supportive diet to strengthen immunity and heal injuries.
It has anti-inflammatory effects and is an essential part of cell membranes.
People don't have to worry about using hemp oil, it doesn't contain any psychoactive substances.
The fact that this oil has found its way to consumers is confirmed by the fact that Bohemia Oil is one of the best-selling companies.
It is sold 500 liters a year.
People often take one spoon in the morning.
Cannabis oil is not pronounced in taste, but it will greatly strengthen immunity, advised Daniel Vlček from the Kraslice company Bohemia Oil.
According to statistics, Americans are the most passionate nation of barbecues.
There are 1.4 grills per household.
There are various competitions in barbecues around the world, which only confirm the success of this culinary discipline.
There aren't Czechs behind either.
On the basis of consumer surveys of the Czech market, we find that only 4% of people did not grill in their lives.
The vast majority grills several times a year.
In order to be successful, we must not underestimate the preparation - it is ideal to adjust the meat by marinating several hours before the heat treatment.
Which oil is most suitable for this and at the same time retains healthy substances when grilling?
In general, during the grilling process itself, fat should be saved.
Experts agree that a large part of the oils are beginning to lose their taste at high temperatures.
Healthy extra virgin oils also lose the body beneficial substances, which we otherwise get from them when consuming oils from dishes prepared at lower temperatures.
However, this does not mean that extra virgin oils do not find their use when grilling.
Grape oil for grilling, health and beauty.
When they say meat, experts from the company Bohemia Oil from Kraslice in the Sokolov region will immediately think of grape oil.
It wonderfully complements the taste of meat and fish.
In the kitchen is characterized by a unique feature of increasing the natural taste of food.
It is also suitable for frying and grilling, because it has a high degree of combustion, up to 216 °C.
Even at such a high temperature, as one of the few oils retains healthy substances, Daniel Vlček describes the benefits of grape oil from Bohemia Olej, which belongs to a few Czech producers of this vine oil.
Grape oil is 50 times more effective than vitamin E and 20 times more efficient than vitamin C.
In addition, it contains a high amount of linoleic acid and is therefore effective in combating excess cholesterol.
In grape oil, our body also receives important unsaturated fatty acids, vitamins and minerals.
Thanks to the favorable content of these substances, it helps to reduce high blood pressure, increases metabolism and has a positive effect on the kidneys.
By consuming grape oil, we also help to increase our external beauty - it improves the elasticity of the skin, is used in the treatment of acne and assists in the care of dry and brittle hair.
Chefs praise the use of grape oil in the kitchen.
Not only is it suitable for the preparation of cold dishes, for example, when flavoring salads, but also for the heat treatment of dishes.
It can be used for grilling in two ways, for marinating and grilling itself.
By marinating meat and fish, we preserve their juiciness.
In the preparation of marinades, three components must be present: oil, acidity and spices.
For example, add acidic acidity with apple cider vinegar and soften the meat.
Spices, in turn, give the meat flavor and the oil preserves and adds the right cut, advises Daniel Vlček.
At the same time, it adds that grapeseed oil is ideal for marining because it is one of the few oils that it can permeate through dark meat.
Marinated meat or fish are ready for grilling, how to proceed?
Extra virgin oils are characterized by the fact that only a few drops are needed to prepare dishes.
The same applies to barbecues.
Some oils are taboo for this method of preparation.
This applies in particular to flax, hemp and rapeseed oil, which should not be heated at all.
Before grilling, rub the grate with oil, so you can prevent the food from burning.
An essential part of grilling is also the preparation of attachments.
Virtually anything is suitable for grilled meat and fish - grilled vegetables, toasted bread, light vegetable salad and many more.
Chefs from Bohemia Olej recommend, for example, hot summer salad.
You need: • 1 peach • 1 bunch of arugula • 1 cup of chopped cucumbers • 1 cup of salad leaf mixture • 3 tablespoons of grape oil
In a salad bowl, add to a mixture of lettuce leaves picked arugula, chopped cucumbers and large cubed peaches.
Salt and pepper to taste, you can also season with ground chilli and soy sauce.
Finally, drizzle with a few drops of grape oil.
For an exceptional taste, you can sprinkle the salad with finely chopped almonds.
Multiple sclerosis: it depends not only on the drugs, but also on the patient's willingness to fight.
Multiple sclerosis is a complicated disease, and a person with this diagnosis needs the care of a number of specialists: a neurologist, physiotherapist, occupational therapist, urologist, ophthalmologist, psychologist, psychiatrist and many other specialists.
However, it is not only medical care, for example, women with multiple sclerosis also need consultations if they decide to have a child, the care of these patients includes social law counseling, recommendations when adjusting housing, etc.
Still, all this is not enough: the development of the disease can be fundamentally influenced by the patient himself.
The more he actively fights the disease, the longer he can work and does not have to fundamentally change the style of his life.
As the doctors point out, the passivity of patients frees up space for the activity of the disease.
For example, it is proven that regular movement greatly delays the time when the patient needs some compensatory aid, for example a stick.
It is important that patients and their surroundings are not subject to various myths, for example, that the disease automatically leads them to end up in a wheelchair.
That’s what’s why the Give Your Chance (www.bezmytu.cz) page (www.bezmytu.cz), which is backed by the ongoing media campaign Have a Chance
The most important person in the care of a patient with multiple sclerosis is a neurologist.
For multiple sclerosis, it is said twice that the sooner the disease begins to be treated, the more likely the doctor may affect something.
This is because we have multiple sclerosis drugs at an inflammatory stage, when the neurodegeneration process isn’t yet so strong.
The sooner we intervene, the greater is the hope that we will be able to stop the disease and delay disability, explains MUDr. Eva Medová from the Neurology Clinic of the General University Hospital in Prague.
It is very important for people with multiple sclerosis rehabilitation care, which most often deals with weakening of the lower limbs or balance disorders.
Patients work according to their individual needs: to maintain fitness, improve walking, strengthen the pelvic floor, reduce swallowing disorders or improve coordination.
"It's really individual, it depends on the patient's specific difficulties," says Martina Kövári, M.D
People with multiple sclerosis have the same disease, but it manifests itself in a slightly different way.
Rehabilitation cannot stop the disease, but it can always alleviate its symptoms.
However, physical activity also strengthens the body's immune state, which is desirable in the case of multiple sclerosis.
Another positive of regular exercise is the fact that the patients verify what they can do, and this strengthens their self-confidence.
"Endorphins are also flushed out during the exercise and a person feels good after it," points out Kamila Řasová from the Department of Rehabilitation Medicine of the University Hospital Royal Vinohrady.
By influencing the physical side, we act on the Limic system responsible for emotions.
Thus, we directly interfere with the psyche and immune processes, and we stabilize the disease, he adds.
"Previously, these patients were saved, today we know that they need a targeted burden," says Prof. PaedDr. Pavel Kolář, Head of the Department of Rehabilitation and Physical Medicine of the University Hospital in Motol.
The aim of physiotherapy is to ensure that a person can remain self-sufficient as long as possible, including job title.
Physiotherapists therefore cooperate with occupational therapists so that each person receives compensatory aid tailored to him.
Many patients also need the care of a psychologist or psychiatrist.
They are in a difficult life situation.
When a serious illness comes into your life, it usually shocks people.
They're experiencing shock, panic, fear.
It has to respond to a large burden - a loss of health.
With such a sore soul, we are supposed to go after someone, not trying to carry everything on our own shoulders.
"I work with them in such a way that they finally come to the conclusion that even with a disability it is possible to live a full life and that multiple sclerosis does not mean the end of life," says psychotherapist Renata Malinová - Schubertová from the Neurological Clinic of the General University Hospital in Prague.
Without the Latecoere manufacturer in Prague, airbuses would not have flowned.
Aviation production is synonymous with precision and advanced technologies.
New aircraft are full of titanium or lightweight and solid composite materials, which can not be manufactured and processed.
Nevertheless, in addition to super-precise, computer-driven machine tools, in addition to autoclaves for shaping composites, you can come across something as ordinary as apricot stones.
In the drum, which resembles a pot for cotton candy, in a pile of stones, the edges of sheet metal parts that have just rolled out of the milling machine.
"So far, no one has come up with anything better," smiles Ivan Dubský, CEO of aeronautical door manufacturer Latecoere Czech Republic.
On the premises in Letňany, Prague, earlier Letov manufactures complete doors for the Airbus A320.
They are the only ones in the world supplying the door for the Brazilian Embraer 170.
Passengers entering the first and upper class on the upper decks of the world's largest Airbus A380 transport aircraft also enter the door, part of which is assembled in Prague.
There are also doors full of composites for the new Boeing 787 Dreamliner.
Accuracy is the main motto here.
For example, the company lets the moment keys be adjusted twice a year.
If there is no record of inspection on the yellow sticker, they should explain in the Prague plant to auditors from Airbus or Boeing, who drive regularly to find out if doors are produced according to the agreed rules.
However, advanced technology has not yet completely replaced the human senses.
There are 1500 rivets on one door to the A320.
You have to shake the rivers by hand.
It'll take them two days.
Even according to the sound of the falling hammer, they can tell if the rivet is already shaken correctly.
The tolerances in which they move are minimal.
The rivy can rise above the surface of the aircraft from zero to 0.13 millimeters.
That's roughly twice the thickness of human hair.
During the inspection, it will be the turn of the trained touch.
When the controller swipes its finger on a row of rivets, he can tell if anyone is out of tolerance.
Only then does he take an accurate indicator in his hand.
Letov fed the L-39 training program before 1989.
In 1991, however, none of them were produced.
The company had to find new orders quickly.
That's when she hooked up with European aircraft manufacturer Airbus.
She won a tender for an emergency door supplier for the A321.
Courtship with Boeing wasn't as happy.
"We were a small company for them at the time, which didn't have enough money for investments and for Boeing to guarantee long-term stable deliveries," Dubský recalls.
The door to the American manufacturer would have been slammed if Letov had not impressed the French group Latecoere at a Prague conference of the international aviation industry association in 1999.
I was talking about our cooperation with Airbus.
Negotiations with the French started the next day, Dubský says.
A year later, Latecoere bought the Czech company and with a strong company came new orders.
As soon as in 2000, the installation of parts of doors for the A320 started.
Three years later, the door of the upper deck for the A380 was added.
In 2006, the company built a new hall for processing composites due to deliveries for the Boeing Dreamliner.
We wouldn't be able to do these big contracts without Latecoer.
Maybe we'd do parts or small parts.
The partners want a guarantee of supplies for twenty or thirty years, Dubský explains.
Last year, Czech Latecoere achieved a turnover of more than 2.9 billion and a profit after tax of 147 million crowns.
An exclusive position among suppliers of aircraft manufacturers is not free.
Latecoere has invested 1.5 billion crowns in Prague since 2000.
The company must have quality certificates, certificates of 170 special production processes and certificates of qualification for key employees.
Without them, the business wouldn't be making any aircraft doors.
Obtaining certificates that the production processes correspond to the requirements of customers, and in repeated inspections to keep them, according to Dubský, cost millions of crowns.
The production processes change every year.
They're more accurate and stricter.
We have to traint employees, retrofit equipment and certify the whole process again, Dubský adds.
Now the company is finalizing the preparation of a process for plating with zinc and nickels, which will replace harmful cadmium for human health.
They got the assignment from the manufacturer, but then they had to adapt the technology for the equipment or chemicals they use in Prague.
The people of Boeing will come, check the concept of the whole line.
Then we'll show them production.
They're going to inspect our lab.
They test one set of samples themselves in their laboratory and then compare the results with ours, approaching Dubský the way in which customers control them.
The reward is long-term exclusive contracts.
The production of embraors stands and falls with the Prague plant today.
For the A320, it produces half of the total door volume.
Replacing the Czech Latecoere is either impossible or very difficult for a Brazilian or European manufacturer.
However, this does not mean that he can say any price at the door.
Part of the contract is a price curve.
It indicates how much one door will cost after ten, fifty, hundred-made pieces.
The price per piece still drops to a certain limit value.
We have to fit into this price pattern.
If we don't, we'll lose, Dubsky says.
Half of the hall where electric cabinets are assembled for an Airbus A400 M military aircraft is still empty.
But it is a symbol of the future.
A new semi-robotic line for riveting and installation of doors for the innovated A320 Neo is being built behind the screen.
Riveting accelerates and refines.
"This is the trend by which assembly in aviation is taking place," adds Dubský.
Sales have a future line secured.
Airbus reports that airlines have so far ordered 3278 units of the new A320.
Just a few meters next to, there will be a line for the complete installation of doors for the A380 upper deck.
It's a strategic decision of our parent company.
The aim is to shorten production times and reduce costs.
Full assembly could begin within two years, Dubský says.
Before that, however, the company has to go through qualifying tests, for example, for the installation of certain electrical and electronic door equipment for the largest Airbus.
The company is also relying on the further development of production from composite materials.
In addition to Boeing, it should also participate in the new Airbus A350 program, which will compete with the American Dreamliner.
"It's a huge credit for the company to process composites in addition to metal materials," Dubsky says proudly.
Latecoere, however, is reaching the edge of production capacities in the Czech Republic.
There is no other place in the Letov area where it resides.
Prior to the entry of the French mother, the company had 180 employees.
Now he has 800 of them, and within three years there could be a hundred more.
As long as Airbus and Boeing are competing, how many hundreds of new planes are being ordered each year, they don't have to worry about their jobs.
Although it has contracts for several years in advance, the parent company Latecoere in Prague faced a threat of bankruptcy.
The French group didn't have enough money for September's loan repayments.
In the end, Latecoere was able to reach an agreement with the main creditors.
At the end of August, part of the loans were exchanged for shares.
The creditors gained a 37.4 percent stake in the company by increasing capital by 57.4 million euros.
The company's debt fell by two-thirds, i.e. by 180 million euros.
The second part of the financial recovery came at the beginning of September.
The company subscribed new shares among existing shareholders for 222.9 million euros.
In total, it raised the share capital by 280 million euros.
At the same time, the group has benefited from the growing production of Airbus and Boeing, which accounts for 85 percent of sales.
It expects average order growth of four percent a year until 2017.
In the custom-made book, it has orders for 2.6 billion euros, equivalent to four-year production.
French media say Latecoere can finally breathe again after years on drips.
The Czech race in Letňany in Prague is important for the groups.
It contributes 16 percent to the group's sales.
According to the number of employees, it is the largest foreign branch of the group.
MPs have backed a larger share of the state from coal charges.
The change in fees for mining will bring 427 million crowns more to the treasury than in 2013.
According to the government, it should have a neutral impact on the revenue of municipal budgets, because the fee is supposed to be higher.
Last year, municipalities received about 450 million crowns from fees and the state budget received 150 million crowns.
About 200 million crowns went to the municipalities and 66 million crowns to the state of brown coal mining.
The amendment also foresees an increase of the payment from the mining areas with allowed mining to a thousand crowns for one hectare per year.
The income from these payments should continue to belong to municipalities in its entirety.
Industry Minister Jan Mládek (ČSSD) told deputies that municipalities will receive 14 million to 100 million crowns a year instead of 14 million.
The amount of mining fees will no longer be determined by law, but stipulated by the government by its regulation.
Reimbursement is newly calculated as the product of the amount of extracted minerals and rates for individual types of minerals.
According to the government, the reason for the change is, among other things, the possibility of a flexible response to the current economic situation.
However, ODS MP Marek Benda warned that setting a fee with government regulations may not comply with the constitution.
However, according to Minister Mládek, it is not a tax in this case, because the state charges the mineral, which is state property.
Fees are given only to municipalities whose territories are affected by mining.
In the case of deep-sea coal mining, three-quarters of the municipality's money and a quarter will be given to the state.
There will be the same ratio in the case of radioactive rock extraction.
A part of the money that the state collects on mining fees will be used on purpose.
For example, 28 percent will have to go to repair the damage after mining or to secure the mining rescue service.
The draft was criticized today by opposition MPs, who argued in particular that it would harm municipalities affected by mining and regions.
For example, Michal Kučera (TOP 09 and Mayors) has warned that mining companies will no longer want to sponsor municipalities as before, because they will pay higher fees directly to the state budget.
"It is not possible to tunnel one of the poorest regions just so that the Minister of Finance improves his budget," said David Kádner (Úsvit), elected in the Ústí region.
KSČM MP Hana Aulická warned against the increase in unemployment in the Most region.
Kádner and Aulická unsuccessfully proposed rejecting the amendment, Kučera wanted to return the law to the government for finalization.
According to mining firms, the increase in fees will not be reflected in coal prices, as prices are more than 90 percent long-term.
Therefore, major consumers such as power plants or heating plants should not feel the increase in prices.
"However, on the other hand, this fact increases the risk that mining organizations will compensate for the increase in reimbursements by trying to reduce their operating expenses, which would primarily mean a reduction in the number of employees," the government admits.
According to her, however, the increase in fees in terms of employment is tolerable.
According to the rapporteur on the amendment by Milan Urban (ČSSD), it is crucial for MPs to know the conclusions about the updated energy concept and, above all, the government's decision on the limits of coal mining.
If coal is mined beyond the limits, it will have an impact on yields for the state and municipalities, he stressed.
Urban disagrees with Mládek that the decision to break the limit at the mine of the Czechoslovak army should fall only after 2020.
According to him, the limits on the CSA mine should be broken already because of social, national economic and because of the long-term stability of domestic energy.
Time to decide on interest rates for the U.S. Federal Reserve
The entire world is watching as the U.S. Federal Reserve prepares to meet in two days on Wednesday and Thursday to make crucial decisions about whether to raise interest rates for the first time in nearly a decade.
A survey of 80 economists interviewed by Reuters found that more than half of those who thought the Federal Reserve would make a decision now think they would remain idle for some time yet and leave interest rates in the range of 0-0.25 percent.
It's a historic event because it's passed the flight from the moment the Fed cut rates to zero.
“For the first time, we are approaching a situation in which a major central bank could be able to get out of zero bar and start the process of normalizing interest rates,” says Angel Ubide, a senior fellow at the Peterson Institute for International Economics.
The U.S. economy did relatively well, there was a recovery in the form of adding trillions of dollars to the state bill and creating only low levels of inflation.
However, the Fed cannot ignore a less rosy global perspective.
They have warned markets to be ready to increase, but circumstances suggest they also see great chances against the move.
The decision is due to be announced on Thursday 20:00 CET.
