Kofola is moving from Poland to the Czech Republic, considering entering the Prague Stock Exchange.
Kofola should have a new headquarters in Ostrava.
Kofola S.A. was registered in Poland because of trading the company's shares on the Warsaw Stock Exchange.
Our primary goal is to have the headquarters of the group in the Czech Republic.
The steps we have taken so far within the project are mainly legal and administrative and do not have a factual impact on events in the company, says Daniel Buryš, finance director of the Kofola Group.
"In connection with the transfer of the group's registered office, shareholders are considering placing shares on the Prague Stock Exchange."
Due to its entry on the Prague Stock Exchange, the company is finalizing a securities prospectus, which it will submit to the Czech National Bank for approval in the near future.
The transfer of the registered office of the holding and the related transfers of shares will be effected in the form of a non-public transaction, provided that only existing shareholders will participate in it.
As part of this operation, therefore, no shares will be offered for subscription to the public or to new investors.
"The eventual offer of shares to new investors would take place - if the company and its shareholders decide to do so - later, either in the fourth quarter of 2015 or in Q1 of 2016," the firm said.
The firm has said in the past that an eventually offer of shares could consist of the issuance of new shares or the sale of existing shares.
This offer could consist of an offer of shares on the stock exchange in the Czech Republic and Poland, including the placement of shares on the Warsaw Stock Exchange.
Test of objectivity of Czech Television in informing about the migrant crisis.
Another small test of objectivity and balance of the coverage of the main Czech media about the refugee crisis.
This time the broadcast of the main news session of Czech Television.
And how did she stand?
When they teach at the faculties of journalism about how the media can manipulate reality, they can release today’s broadcast of Czech Television Events.
About 80% of news coverage was dedicated to the migrant crisis.
It wasn't until the first minute, when ČT reported on riots on the Serbian-Hungarian border and the attacks of migrants on policemen euphemistically ran out of patience - throwing rocks and attacking with metal sticks), had already ridden the current pro-migrant propaganda - judge for yourself the names of the individual reports.
Criticism of NGOs - a large space for non-profit organizations that criticise the mistreatment of migrants.
Syrian children at the Czech school - the story of integrated Syrians in the Czech Republic.
Refugees not only as a threat, but also as a chance.
Wandering refugees - ČT consistently uses the terms refugee or refugee and not a migrant.
What is striking is that ČT consistently uses shots for young children and women in illustration shots.
In the same broadcast, she herself said that of the migrants detained in the Czech Republic, 80% are men.
Summary: For the most part propaganda that is unparalleled from communist agities.
I have to say, as a former journalist, I'm ashamed of my colleagues.
Ecology in practice.
When I once reached a block of flats, I soon ceased to be the only resident.
I had fish moved into my umakarta toilet.
Pound, insects with an imperfect transformation, i.e., which does not lose the transformation from caterpillar to beetle and cub looks like an adult individual, only it is tiny and grows gradually.
They were disgusting to me and I didn't lazy to kill them.
First by hand and later chemically.
The socialist drugstore for their liquidation provided a kind of blue crystals.
I think it was called Cyclone B.
Or something else?
However, it eliminated them successfully.
Later I did the same thing with the pharaohs.
A box with a kind of juvenalizer, which the ants brought to their nest, and he then did not allow the queen to generate new offspring.
But that's what I've turned.
As time went on, insects became an object of my admiration, and more and more I was inclined to think that they had the same right to life as we humans.
In addition, I took away from my life the experience that interfering with the ecosystem does not lead to success, and one pest can replace the other.
I don't think I'd hesitate to exacerbate karma by killing them.
In the new residence, my partner and I agreed that if we don’t have ponds crawling behind our necks, let them calmly eat crispoons of fallen skin, some invisible algae and the like.
After a while, their peaceful existence was disturbed by a spider.
It was a common kind of fool who had long resided on the ceiling.
We thought he lived off occasional flies and mosquitoes, which only increased our comfort.
Because he spent several years with us, we found out that he mainly feeds on ponds and that he probably kept their number in a bearable numerical state.
By intimate regular contact at every need performed, we discovered that it was a female.
We have witnessed romantic conversations with a partner of about a third smaller, how carefully he tingles on the fibers of the cobweb, so that it is not eaten before he achieves the coveted copulation.
It took about three days when they didn't move and didn't even respond to our controls.
Under the toilet bowl, where love games took place, we later finded the remains of a dried male next to the female.
Then the spider didn't move for weeks.
When we thought it was over, we were surprised by a number of small spiders hanging around her.
They soon disappeared.
They were eaten by their mommy, they scattered elsewhere.
Even after a week, the female disappeared somewhere.
Whether she'd gone somewhere else or died, we don't know that, but after a month or two, she showed up on the ceiling again.
That's right, a little smaller, probably the daughter of that bathroom resident.
For some time from the ceiling cautiously observed our behavior and by moving under the toilet bowl evaluated our non-aggression as a friendship.
The numerical status of somewhat multiplied ponds decreased again, and the spider calmly stared at its normal activities to provide food.
Our ecosystem hasn't changed for a year.
In the meantime, our daughter reached an age when the use of potty was an embarrassment.
We have tolerated it until now, but the eternal pouring out of its contents has already been eaten.
We urged her more and more emphatically to use the toilet.
The daughter, however, found an excuse in that spider, which she saw very well when wiping.
Our talk about seeing the spider didn't take luck in the house at all.
Crying and roaring forced her potty.
There was no choice.
There was a moment when the spider, in the interest of the daughter's developmental shift, had to command.
It's up to me.
He was caught in a jar and banished across the balcony somewhere in the garden.
I said good-bye to him as a friend, but I still felt nasty after cohabiting like I'd been throwing out a relative.
We anticipated that the ponds would start appearing more often and begin to multiply with a geometric series.
Surprising the world, for a week or two, we didn't have any there.
I started speculating about the cause.
I wondered if the spider had somehow grown there after the ant pattern, that the toilet environment wasn't as favorable for their existence as we'd thought.
But then the first pieces of medium-size appeared, and they swarmed again.
I had to come up with a different theory about the cause of their disappearance, and I found out that their connection to the spider had to have a cause in that if they didn't see it, that it was hidden in some other place, and that they were in danger from anywhere.
Or, maybe they had some kind of telepathic connection with their predator, and its rapid disappearance triggered some kind of alarming reaction.
I have no illusions about their eyesight.
Some shy light showed shyness, but that they would react to waving their hands or fast movements, it didn't.
My daughter goes to the bathroom regularly.
I think she's already forgotten the potty.
All that's left is to attract a spider again.
I'm already sending my wish to the ether and I hope they didn't give up on me after the foreclosure.
Otherwise we'd have to use the Cyclone B.
The Ten Statements of Albert Einstein, which enriched the world.
The statements of a genius scientist from the last century will probably never cease to fascinate humanity.
He was able to dip into everything so deeply that the figment was always an astonishing finding.
Albert Einstein (1879 - 1955) was one of the most important scientists of all time.
In particular, he became aware of people with his special and general theory of relativity, which so far best describes the universe in its gigantic ratio.
It is also impossible to omit its clarification of the photo-effect or the idea of quanting the electromagnetic field.
There is no doubt that the description itself and the system of knowledge of the popular theory of relativity is so intricate for many that it prefers to choose easy arcades for a closer acquaintance.
However, it is not easy.
But it wouldn’t have been Albert Einstein if he hadn’t found a brilliantly simplistic form of explanation for this, too: A watch near your sweetheart seems a minute; a minute in a hot oven seems an hour – and that’s relativity.
I took the liberty of selecting these tens from his entire variety of famous quotes, which literally captivated me.
Intelligent people try to solve problems, genius tries not to do them.
Only two things are endless.
The universe and human stupidity.
I'm not so sure about the first one.
No number of attempts can ever prove that I was right.
The only one, however, can prove I was wrong at any time.
But it's a sad time when it's easier to break up an atom than to destroy prejudice.
If the mess on the table is a reflection of disorder in the mind, then what reflects an empty table?
I don't know what it's going to be fought in World War III, but it'll be sticks and stones in the fourth.
There are thousands of ways to kill time, but none to resurrect it.
Knowing little is dangerous and knowing a lot too.
If I had an hour to handle the problem on which my life would depend, I would spend 40 minutes studying it, 15 minutes analyzing it, and 5 minutes solving it.
In the world, the hardest thing to understand income tax.
In conclusion, I cannot forgive myself not to put Einstein's formula on the definition of success: Taking A for success: A=X+Y+Z, where X is work, Y rest, and Z is to keep your mouth shut.
New and modern.
Hospitals in the Zlin region are expecting changes for 1.5 billion.
"It's a success when we consider that this whole year, all fours are sticking in black numbers," said Stanislav Mišák.
The total profit of regional facilities at the moment is about 32 million crowns.
This is mainly due to higher payments from insurance companies, which are equally favorable for this year.
Even this fact shows that after poor years, hospitals can finally afford more investment.
In Kroměříž, Vsetín, Uherské Hradiště and Zlín, thanks to this, constructions that together will cost almost 1.5 billion crowns.
The long period, when we bought mainly instruments, was over.
Now we have to start building new buildings, because without them it is not possible to do top-class health care, the regional deputy for the health service Lubomír Nečas justified the plans.
He is looking forward to changes in all hospitals.
Builders will come to hospitals next year.
In Vsetín, suppliers of a new internal pavilion are now being selected for almost 300 million crowns.
In Kroměříž they have planned an extension of dialysis.
Uherské Hradiště wants to add a new intern for about 200 million to this year's central pavilion.
And Baťa’s hospital in Zlín is waiting for the long-delayed construction of a new central income and an interna, for which three quarters of a billion will be needed.
In all cases, these are fundamental and often the biggest changes in recent years.
"This is an extremely important step for the whole region, patients and doctors," Věra Prousková, the hospital's director, said about the construction of the Vsetín intern.
The five-storey building is supposed to be finished there in about two years and offers comfortable equipment for intern and neurology, dialysis, new ambulances, beds and intensive care unit.
More comfort for patients.
Changes, which will be significantly recognized mainly by patients, will affect all regions.
New buildings will replace those in which, for example, many patients lie in one room, have only one toilet on the floor, beds are unpositionable, leaky windows and paramedics do not have adequate conditions for work.
"For example, our intern was built thirty-five years ago and is now at the limit of its service life," said Pavel Calábek, director of the Zlín hospital.
Within a few years it will be replaced by a seven-storey modern building connected with an urgent reception.
Doctors and patients will have all acute wards in one place, in addition, in new premises.
The same model already has halved Uherské Hradiště.
The central income is already standing and within three years there will be an intern.
"We will pay for the construction from the loan and partly from our own funds," explained director Petr Sládek.
It is precisely this hospital that can afford its own funding in the county.
The profit is still the highest and did not make a loss two years ago, when, for example, the Zlín hospital struggled with an almost two-hundred-million-dollar loss.
"We have good contracts with insurance companies, excellent performance, we increase revenues and effectively manage costs throughout the hospital," said Vlastimil Vajdák, who is in charge of the economy.
There will also be an improvement in patients of the Kroměříž hospital.
Within ten to fifteen years, up to half a billion crowns will go into repairs, new devices and renovations.
Already this year will be the repair of the detention station, then the extension of the dialysis will begin, or the construction of the building for a new magnetic resonance.
