FastMig X is a representative of the latest generation of inverter welding resources.
The combination of state-of-the-art technology, hardware and software integrated into modular design brings benefits and a quick return on investment in the form of high quality, productivity and reliability.
FastMig X is a modular system, therefore the final assembly is always configured according to customer requirements.
And any of this, from the welding of structural steel to the welding of special alloys, as well as from the welding of coarse materials to the welding of thin sheets, from applications in workshops to welding in shipyards.
An incredible number of welding curves, simple adjustment and extendability of the welding source allows you to react quickly to a change in requirements, which leads to a reduction in downtime, the need to rearrange the source and more productive welding.
FastMig X allows welding by cutting-edge welding processes developed by Kemppi, which ensure higher productivity and welding quality.
It stops wasting time and there is no waste of materials or correction of faulty welds.
Flexibility is ensured, there is less downtime, more welding and higher profit.
It's this year's news, which premiered in Nitra, where it also won a gold medal.
We greatly appreciate these honors because they confirm the uniqueness of the product.
The world's leading manufacturers boast similar systems, but due to the difference in software and in parameter control, FastMig X is one of the world leaders.
For those interested are also pleasant delivery times, which are around three weeks.
In the Czech Republic, we have already established the first contacts, which will definitely expand after the Brno trade fair.
We have been its regular participants for more than twenty years and almost always our business results are better than before it, emphasizes Miroslav Streichsbier on behalf of ARC-H, the manager of Kemppi in Pilsen.
