Brazilian Pediatric Society Rio Grande Promotes Healthy Dieting While Breastfeeding
The Brazilian pediatric company SPRS has come up with a shocking way to try to convey to women knowledge about the importance of a good diet while breastfeeding using pictures of babies sucking from their breasts painted by displaying unhealthy food.
Human breast milk consists of different proteins, fats, vitamins and carbohydrates, which give infants all the nutrients they need to create a strong immune system.
Thanks to a lot of energy requirements, pregnant women and new mothers are advised to increase their daily calorie intake by 500 calories a day.
However, new surveys suggest that increased calorie intake is not the only dietary precaution that mothers should follow.
A recent study conducted by Robert Waterland, a professor at Baylor College of Medicine in Texas, found that the healthy diets of pregnant women actually impacted their children's genetic formation and protected them from the development of tumors.
Unfortunately, unhealthy diets were also confirmed to negatively affect children's immune systems.
