Peeter Moody accused the Racing Victoria organisers of trying to get into his stable last year and threatened to end racing immediately.
He focused on the organisers and integrity department of Racing Victoria and was based on the belief that Lady Tatai's late scratch campaign had a personal campaign against him during maintenance on the day of the race, which was the last straw for him on Wednesday.
Moody told Fairfax Media that he was always trying to do what was best for racing and found himself in a difficult situation when it comes to Lidar's positive swab on cobalt that he couldn't explain.
He bit his tongue about espionage charges for 18 months and didn't want it to look like "dry grapes."
