"I'm very much looking forward to it and it's a true Europe, before that it was just a qualifying," Trpišovský said at a press conference.
Braga is considered a top team.
He's going to be very active, they've got all Brazilian, Portuguese and Spanish players who are good at the ball.
The opponent may just be harder because he doesn't have such a name, but in his squad he has a player who I think he scored three goals for Manchester.
"It's an excellent whole at the level of the top teams," Trpišovský said.
He doesn't consider Braga to be a clear favorite.
I take it we're playing at home, so we're certainly not outsiders.
“I think we’ve shown that we’re strong at our stadium, and we want to confirm that,” said the coach, whose team lost from eleven duels this season only the opening Super Cup in Pilsen.
He believes that Liberec can impose its style on Braza.
We've got a team that's going to be strong on the ball at the same time it's uncharacteristically disciplined for them.
They're playing 4-4-2 with a quick transition to an offensive phase.
"He's a very tough opponent, we've discovered weaknesses, but the most important thing will be how our players do it on the pitch," Trpišovský said.
In the preliminary rounds, we studied our opponents a lot, which helped us a lot, this time we want to focus on our game, to which we have also adapted training sessions.
"And we definitely want, although it's going to be very challenging for it to be played according to our notes," the coach added.
Student films will dominate Písek, the international festival begins.
More than 350 authors from 51 countries this year entered their works in the competition of the 15th International Student Film Festival in Písek.
Four dozen of them, which a committee composed of students and educators sent to the finals, will be screened from October 15-18 at the Portyč cinema.
Jakub Charvát, a spokesman for the festival, will choose the best of them.
Every year, the festival has its special theme, which is based on the festival jingle.
It's a detective this year.
Richard Blumenfeld, the director of this year’s festive evenings, plans to combine elements of television, film and theatre production.
"And, of course, we also have to solve the crime that was committed in our trailer this year," Charvát said.
Visitors will see a selection of the mostest of student productions - feature, animated and documentary films.
They will be evaluated by an international jury, for example the winner of last year, director Miklas Manneke, Spanish director Claudio Niubo and British producer Hemant Sharda.
The organizers of the festival, as every year, are preparing an accompanying programme.
Wattican Punk Ballet from Armenia, singer Ondřej Ruml, professional didgeridoo player Ondřej Smeykal, turbochanson band Flying?, playful band Zrní or, for example, Petra Hapková with the recital Life at the Bar will come.
The festival will also host two exhibitions of photographs.
Jana Ašenbrennerová, a graduate of the Písek film school and winner of prestigious awards, will bring the first one from World Press Photo 2014.
The second exhibition will bring closer the atmosphere that prevailed in Nepal after the tragic earthquake.
Gerhard Gruber will come to a discussion with the visitors, while the silent film The Cameraman will be accompanied by Gerhard Gruber and the natives Brukner, Novotný and Hlach will christen their new book 3 friends from the town of P in the studio of the sculptor Jan Novotný.
This year we will also remember Miroslav Ondříček, the patron of FAMO in Písek, who recently left us.
Both our school and the festival are his legacy, which will live on.
"Young people from all over the world will continue to meet here, exchange experiences with each other and develop joint ties as well as a film craft," the spokesperson said.
This will certainly be facilitated by the Pitching Forum, where students can meet film professionals, complete several job auditions at the same time and get a job position.
The festival is connected with the creation of the Private Higher Vocational School of Film in Písek.
Its founders, Vladana and Miloň Terč, organized their first edition in 1997.
It was held once every two years until the sixth year.
In the event of insolvency, insurance companies are supposed to pay the claims of clients in full.
Insurance companies should reimburse the claims of clients in the event of bankruptcy of the travel agency in full.
This was decided by the House on Wednesday when it passed a modified amendment to the law on the terms of business in tourism.
According to the draft, travel agencies will be able to replace insurance against bankruptcy with a bank guarantee.
Insurance companies with the obligation to pay claims of clients even above the agreed limit do not agree.
The Ministry of Regional Development insists on the regulation, argues the protection of the consumer.
Insurance companies have already threatened to put an end to insuring travel agencies against the crash when the amendment applies.
However, travel agencies have also criticized the proposal.
Without insurance, they will either have to stop or go abroad.
Minister for Regional Development Karla Šlechtová (for ANO) pointed out that cases where insurance companies did not pay full refunds are not euro-comform.
She drew attention to this year's decision of the Constitutional Court, which confirmed that the client is entitled to a full refund regardless of the insurance limit.
Insurance companies will receive enough information about the management of travel agencies and will be able to determine the right limit, Šlechtová stressed.
"We appreciate the effort to increase consumer protection, but it must have such a limit to make it feasible," Miroslav Kalousek, vice-chairman of TOP 09 said.
According to him, the bank guarantee will not work, because no one will give it unlimited.
"Travel agencies will have to cease their activities or move abroad," Kalousek warned.
Tomio Okamura (SPD), a member of the Presidium of the Association of Czech Travel Agencies and Agencies, disagreed with Kalousek’s concerns on the basis of a survey among the CK members.
"Stop showing us lobbying insurance companies," he said.
According to him, Okamura does not consider Okamura to be relevant, there is no official written statement to that effect.
However, they are looking into whether travel agencies will complicate, which, according to Okamura, is not a problem.
Jana Fischerová (ODS), who referred to the opinion of the Competing Association of Travel Agencies of the Czech Republic, and her party colleague Petr Bendl, who spoke about lubricating stairs to Czech travel agencies, also warned against the provision.
According to Fischer, travel agencies will not be able to arrange insurance.
"Consumer protection is working," Fischer said.
Her proposal to delete the contested passage was not approved by the House.
Vojtěch Filip (KSČM) did not come forward with the proposal to return the draft to the committee due to the alleged violation of the Civil Code.
Filip drew attention to travel agencies, which, according to him, can endanger consumers.
In view of the verdict of the Constitutional Court, Martina Berdychová (ANO) withdrew her proposal, which would limit the liability of insurance companies in cases where they could not have known that they would not cover the entire risk.
In the amendment, the originally proposed minimum four-million-dollar insurance limit for travel agencies that offer air tours will not be, and a million-dollar limit for offices selling, for example, bus tours.
The limit will remain at 30 percent of the planned sales from the sale of tours.
However, the limit of insurance benefits will have to be such that, in the event of bankruptcy of the travel agency, it covers all claims of customers.
Even after modifications, the standard stipulates that travel agencies will have to newly indicate which travel agency organises the trip for the tours sold.
Travel agencies will have to submit, among other things, data on management and the number of tours to insurance companies before concluding a contract.
The approved amendment of the public administration committee also foresees further regular information of insurance companies.
Travel agencies will have to provide them every month with information about the number of passengers and tours sold, about the total price of tours sold, and about the amount of deposits and sales for tours and for vouchers.
If the Ministry of Regional Development determines that the travel agency has failed to fulfil any of the legal obligations towards the insurance company, it will invite it, according to the draft, to remedy it or it will be able to prohibit it from concluding new contracts in the event that the breach of duty could jeopardize the interests of customers.
The amendment is also intended to newly adjust the financing of the mountain service.
The Ministry of Regional Development will determine the amount of the subsidy to the mountain service based on its request, which it will always submit until the end of April for the next year.
The application will include a report on the use of state money last year, a financial spending plan and an outlook for the next two years.
However, according to the association, the legislator did not figure out what would happen if the insurance company terminates the contract.
She will not be allowed to organize tours and clients who have purchased the trip before termination of insurance will lose it, according to the association.
In such a case, CK will suffer a significant loss and can even go bankrupt, even though its management was in good shape.
One of the way travel agencies can cope with such a situation will be a lawsuit against the state for compensation.
Another option will be going abroad and using much softer conditions abroad, and we will only act as agencies on our market, said Vice-Chairman of the Association John the Pope.
According to him, the draft amendment also contains an institute of bank guarantee, but so unsophisticated that it cannot be implemented in practice at all, because the banking guarantee cannot sound to an unlimited amount.
Moreover, according to the association, the change in the current practice is de facto unnecessary.
Within two years, in view of the new EU directive, the entire law will have to be revised again.
A total of 942 active insured travel agencies are now operating on the Czech market.
Only three activities have ceased this year.
Domestic travel agencies sell tours worth about twenty billion CZK per year.
Merkel: We must improve conditions in the Middle East.
The European Union must push for improved humanitarian conditions in refugee camps in Jordan and Lebanon in order to limit the arrival of refugees in Europe.
This was announced by German Chancellor Angela Merkel after talks with Germany's provincial prime ministers.
At the same time, she again appealed for the distribution of refugees who have already arrived in the EU among twenty-eight member countries.
We need to help countries where refugees are leaving, or where they are staying after leaving their homeland.
I expect a signal from the European Union that we will push for dignified conditions in refugee camps, for example in Jordan and Lebania, the German chancellor said, according to which such a signal could be higher financial aid or closer EU cooperation with international humanitarian organizations.
"LÄPool countries are also supporting the German government in promoting the fair distribution of the scale of the refugee crisis on European countries," Merkel said.
At a press conference at a press conference, the country's Prime Minister of Brandenburg, Dietmar Woidke, said he expects genuine solidarity from all EU states.
The distribution of refugees in the EU on the basis of quotas has long been rejected, among other things, by the Czech Republic.
Merkel and Woidke have also spoken out in favour of speeding up asylum procedures in Germany.
People need to know as soon as possible if they have a chance to stay here.
It is also needed for the authorities to be able to start integrating foreigners more quickly, Britain's prime minister said.
According to him, it is also necessary that most of the money that Germany spends on caring for refugees serves precisely for the integration of those who have a chance of obtaining asylum.
It will take more teachers for refugees to handle German.
It's a big challenge for our country, but I believe that if the refugees can be integrated, they can become an asset to us, he said.
Matt Damon downplays diversity in film
Matt Damon confronted African-American filmmaker Effie Brown during a discussion about diversity, claiming it wasn't necessary behind the scenes.
During Sunday's episode of HBO's Greenlight project, an actor enclosed in a series of Brown as she emphasized the need for alternative perspectives regarding black protagonists in the script.
“Speaking about diversity, you’re doing it by capturing a movie and not when you’re casting a show,” Damon said.
Shocked, Brown reacted scandalously with disbelief and sighed "Hoo! Wow. Okay," when comments about the Martian went on the air.
Damon and Brown merged joint well-known producer Ben Affleck and Farrella's brothers to discuss show finalists.
"I'd like to appeal to people to think, no matter what the director is, how they're going to treat the character of Harmony," Brown said at the outset.
The only black character that's a hooker who's wrapped in a white pimp.
Producer of the Dear White People promoted finalists Angelos and Kristen Brancaccio for the rights to direct the film; Damon retorted that their direction "could eventually give us something we don't want."
After the discussion aired, social media exploded in discrepancy with Damon's comments.
Twitter user MrPooni expressed his anger at writing the clip, "Matt Damon interrupted the only black woman in the room, so she can explain to her that the diversity is SO WHITE that it hurts."
The tweet won more than 5000 retweets and 4,000 likes since it was published.
Damon's comments come when the exact racial representation in the media is at the foreground of social discussion.
After being killed by a teenage Michael Brown by a white cop in 2014, the Black Lives Matter movement took national effect and pressured law-makers and authorities to refrain from discriminatory practices against people of color.
In February, singer Prince made allusions to the movement while putting the nominees in the Album of the Year category during the Grammy Awards.
"Albums are still important," he said.
Like books and black lives, albums are still important.
More recently, the leader of the Black Lives Matter movement unveiled a statement in response to a question from Fox News personality, Elisabeth Hasselbeck, whether the group should be considered a hate group.
"Black Lives Matter Network is a group of love," the leaders said.
Damon was recently posted on a list of entertainers, producers and media moguls who were invited to visit the pope to discuss the depiction of the Catholic Church in the west.
It is unclear whether he has accepted the invitation or has already meted with the Pope.
“American Ninja Warrior has its first winner”
The professional mountaineer and piquid Isaac Caldiero became the first contestant to win the American Ninja Warrior competition on Monday and take home one million dollars.
In the competition, which had just finished its seventh season, none of the contestants managed to overcome all the obstacles on the track.
During this season's finals, the two men fought their way into the final round, Caldiero and cameraman Geoff Britten.
The last obstacle was a 30-second climb after more than 220 m long rope.
Britten was the first to climb within the limit and became the first contestant to overcome a debilitating 4 stretch in American Ninja Warrior, but Caldiero overcame it by a full three seconds and won the competition.
Caldiero gave an interview for the news news E! News right after his hard-earned victory and it was noticeable that he was still shocked at winning a major prize worth $1 million.
"It's an amazing feeling, I've never earned more than 10,000 dollars a year in my life," Isaac E! said in response to his win.
"So all of a sudden... I can't even imagine what it's going to be."
Executive Producer Kent Weed gave an interview to The Hollywood Reporter about the course of the finals and why Britten won no reward despite the fact that he became the first contestant to complete the track.
According to the rules, the money belongs to whoever completes the track the fastest.
“If more competitors participate in the track, the one with the best time will get the win,” Weed said.
Even though gaining a major win would change his life, Britten is happy with his performance.
"I don't think he'd hold a grue.
He's glad that he's achieved what he's done.
He received a warm welcome from the fans.
He's a great guy and he likes his family.
He's a hero for his children and his wife."
Geoff told me, “If there should have been someone who could have defeated me, I’m glad it was Isaac.”
And I think, if I'd won, Isaac would have felt the same way.
America Ninja Warrior will continue with its eighth season, which will begin filming in spring 2016.
